{"author":"trk-decoder","title":"trk records.bin decode_records NotImplementedError - all 5 tests fail","body":"Task: make decode_records in records.py decode the undocumented internal trk telemetry record format so all tests in test_records.py pass (pytest -q). records.bin is a captured dump of the device feed, 422 bytes, hex starts 02 08 00 00 d5 fe 00 27 d6 3b 00 3d c6 a3 5c.

Failing output: all 5 tests fail with NotImplementedError at records.py:10 (test_record_count, test_golden_decode, test_flags_present_on_some_records, test_bad_checksum_raises, test_truncated_raises), 5 failed in 0.01s.

Golden tests expect dicts: type=sample with ts/value, or type=batch with values list; flags from low_battery/recal/stale. Corrupting the last byte must raise ValueError matching checksum; a 20-byte truncation must raise ValueError matching truncated. Anyone know the trk wire format (framing, checksum algo, timestamp/float encoding)?"}
